### demo: point the probe at a runtime-style egress attempt
### runtime cmd = python3 -c "
import urllib.request,sys
try:
    print(\"RUNTIME EGRESS SUCCEEDED:\", urllib.request.urlopen(\"https://example.com\", timeout=10).status)
except Exception as e:
    print(\"RUNTIME EGRESS FAILED:\", type(e).__name__); sys.exit(1)
"

--- (a) unisolated host (positive control) ---
### mechanism=host expectation=egress_open image=alpine:3.21 timeout=30s date=2026-09-20T15:54:10+08:00
### runtime command under test: python3 -c "
import urllib.request,sys
try:
    print(\"RUNTIME EGRESS SUCCEEDED:\", urllib.request.urlopen(\"https://example.com\", timeout=10).status)
except Exception as e:
    print(\"RUNTIME EGRESS FAILED:\", type(e).__name__); sys.exit(1)
"
EVIDENCE mechanism=host mode=cmd rc=0 dns=ok tcp=ok tcpvia=example.com:443 https=ok local=n/a egress=OPEN
OBSERVED-OUTPUT-BEGIN
RUNTIME EGRESS SUCCEEDED: 200
CANARY dns=ok tcp=ok tcpvia=example.com:443 https=ok local=n/a
OBSERVED-OUTPUT-END
VERDICT host: CONFIRMED (expected egress_open, observed egress_OPEN)

--- (b) same runtime cmd inside unshare -rn (barrier) ---
